    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 85,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "The CardBERT space clusters this deck mostly by card TYPE and colour, not by job: artifacts (city-0), blue draw and tutors (city-1), lands (city-2), white spells (city-3), counters (city-4), enchantments (city-5). The frame's three legs are spread across those types: table draw sits in city-0 (Howling Mine, Font of Mythos, Temple Bell, Horn of Greed), city-1 (Kami of the Crescent Moon, The Second Doctor, Kwain) and city-1-hood-2 (Dictate of Kruphix); the fort is split between city-5 and city-3 (Archangel of Tithes). The names describe what each city does; none of them should be read as 'the group-hug leg'.",
      "city-4's fallback 'Bodies' (and its hood's 'Bodies II') is wrong: the city holds six counterspells and Cyclonic Rift, with no creature. Swan Song is its verified card (stack 002).",
      "city-4 and city-5 each have exactly one neighbourhood with the same cards as the city, so the hood cannot be narrower. They are labelled ('COUNTERS PLUS A RESET', 'STANDING ENCHANTMENTS') only so the renderer does not show the misleading fallbacks. A renderer could reasonably hide a single-hood city's hood.",
      "Odd members: Teferi's Ageless Insight (a personal draw doubler) sits in THE FORT because it is an enchantment, not because it defends; Isochron Scepter sits with the any-colour mana sources and is not one; Karametra's Blessing sits with the artifact and enchantment removal; Braingeyser lands among the creatures in BODIES THAT DRAW, not with the other X-draw spells in hood-0; Arcane Denial and An Offer You Can't Refuse are counters filed under the tutors, likely because both hand opponents cards. Approach of the Second Sun sits with the white removal and wraths (city-3-hood-0), which is why that city's name carries 'THE EXIT'.",
      "city-2-hood-1 reads clean: Hallowed Fountain, Irrigated Farmland and Prairie Stream all carry the Plains and Island types, with the two basics. city-2-hood-0 is the remainder (slow, check and pain duals, the two channel lands, Signet, Talisman, Skycloud Expanse)."
    ]
  },
